@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+# Partner reputation / QoS
+
+Evidence-based profiles for **buyers** and **transport agencies**. Code: `backend/app/services/reputation.py` (rules), `backend/app/routers/reputation.py` (API), `frontend/src/pages/Partners.jsx` / `MyReputation.jsx`.
+
+## Rules (the point of the module)
+- Every figure is computed from rows that already exist. Nothing is defaulted, seeded, smoothed or estimated. The legacy `Buyer.reliability_score` / `payment_history_score` columns are seeded defaults and are **never read**.
+- Each indicator shows `numerator / denominator` and its latest event. No evidence → `not_recorded` (never 0 %, never a penalty).
+- Fewer than 3 completed outcomes → **"Insufficient history"**, never a low score.
+- Evidence a partner has contested (OPEN / UNDER_REVIEW / UPHELD) is excluded from their rates and counted separately; a REJECTED dispute counts again.
+- Simulated (demo) payments are never counted. Open complaints are shown as counts, not penalties.
+- No composite score. Ordering uses the 95 % Wilson lower bound, so a 5/5 record ranks below 95/100.
+- Thresholds (grace period, quote tolerance, minimum history) are tunable policy parameters, not measured results.
+
+## Who records what
+| Evidence | Recorded by | Endpoint | Guard |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Buyer pickup (ON_TIME / LATE / NO_SHOW) and terms (AS_AGREED / DEVIATED) | the farmer on the transaction | `POST /reputation/records` | only after goods have moved (PICKED_UP onwards); one per metric per transaction; buyer is notified |
+| Final transport charge | the trip's farmer | `POST /reputation/transport/{id}/final-charge` | only after delivery, once |
+| Delivery promise | farmer or the trip's agency | `POST /reputation/transport/{id}/delivery-promise` | only before pickup, once (API only; no UI yet) |
+| Who cancelled a trip | automatic | farmer cancel/status endpoints, transporter status endpoint | legacy rows stay `NULL` and are never blamed |
+
+## Right of reply
+A rated partner contests one specific item (`POST /reputation/disputes`, own evidence only). An admin sets UNDER_REVIEW / UPHELD / REJECTED (`PATCH /reputation/admin/disputes/{id}`); a written reason is required to decide.
+
+## Link to negotiation
+A `BUYER_TERMS` outcome is measured against the agreement snapshot written when the offer was accepted (`offer_agreements`, SHA-256 fingerprint). The fingerprint is included in the transaction timeline event and in the buyer's evidence view, so the buyer sees what they are being measured against.
+
+## Demo data
+`python -m app.mock_data.seed_qos_demo` (from `backend/`) creates 12 demo partners whose *evidence* exercises every UI state; `--reset` removes it. Profiles are still computed by the real service.
+
+## Known limits
+- Reputation reflects CropRetain activity only; it is not a guarantee of future performance.
+- Buyer outcomes depend on farmers recording them. Transport agencies are not notified when a final charge is recorded (no transporter notification channel exists yet); they see it under My Reputation.
+- UI strings for the reputation feature are translated for English, Hindi, Marathi and Bengali only; the other 11 locales currently contain the English text.
